{"code_citation":"Cal. Civ. Code § 4900","title":"Open meeting requirement; board actions in executive session","category":"meetings","body":"Any member of the association may attend meetings of the board, except when the board adjourns to, or meets solely in, executive session to consider litigation, matters relating to the formation of contracts, member discipline, personnel matters, or to meet with a member, upon the member's request, regarding the member's payment of assessments. SAMPLE EXCERPT — replace with full statutory text from leginfo.legislature.ca.gov before production use.","source_url":"https://leginfo.legislature.ca.gov/faces/codes_displaySection.xhtml?lawCode=CIV&sectionNum=4900.","effective_date":null}
{"code_citation":"Cal. Civ. Code § 5605","title":"Limits on special assessments","category":"assessments","body":"The board may not impose a regular assessment that is more than 20 percent greater than the regular assessment for the preceding fiscal year, or impose special assessments which in the aggregate exceed 5 percent of the budgeted gross expenses of the association for that fiscal year, without the approval of a majority of a quorum of members of the association at a properly noticed member meeting. SAMPLE EXCERPT — replace with full statutory text before production use.","source_url":"https://leginfo.legislature.ca.gov/faces/codes_displaySection.xhtml?lawCode=CIV&sectionNum=5605.","effective_date":null}
{"code_citation":"Cal. Civ. Code § 5650","title":"Assessment liens","category":"foreclosure","body":"A regular or special assessment, and any late charges, reasonable costs of collection, attorney's fees, and interest assessed in accordance with Section 5650, shall be a debt of the owner of the separate interest at the time the assessment or other sums are levied. At any time after the assessment becomes delinquent, the association may record a lien on the owner's separate interest. SAMPLE EXCERPT — replace with full statutory text before production use.","source_url":"https://leginfo.legislature.ca.gov/faces/codes_displaySection.xhtml?lawCode=CIV&sectionNum=5650.","effective_date":null}
{"code_citation":"Cal. Civ. Code § 4775","title":"Maintenance and repair responsibilities","category":"architectural","body":"Unless otherwise provided in the declaration, the association is responsible for repairing, replacing, and maintaining the common area, other than exclusive use common area, and the owner of each separate interest is responsible for repairing, replacing, and maintaining that separate interest. SAMPLE EXCERPT — replace with full statutory text before production use.","source_url":"https://leginfo.legislature.ca.gov/faces/codes_displaySection.xhtml?lawCode=CIV&sectionNum=4775.","effective_date":null}
